From 0e00d355a4a1e91b40b6cea7b1eb8dbd402d0203 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 14:38:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ship): auto-start the constant PR monitor on ship
 success
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add lib/pr-monitor/watch-lifecycle.js: startPrWatcherDetached spawns a detached,
unref'd `forge shepherd watch <pr>` — non-blocking and idempotent (best-effort
slug+watcherRunning probe skips a live watcher; the watch loop's own PID guard is
the authoritative de-dup). It NEVER throws: a spawn/gh failure degrades to
'not started'.

Wire into ship via maybeStartPrWatcher (executeShip, after prNumber is known):
skipped on dry-run/no-pr and wrapped so a watcher failure can NEVER fail ship.
Extracted as a small exported seam so the guard is unit-testable without live gh.

Epic c2d398e5-26cf-4963-b47a-70b4102636bb (PR-B).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
